<BaseLayout title="About">
  <h1>About</h1>

  <p>
    I am a PhD student in the school of Electrical and Electronic Engineering at 
    Nanyang Technological University (NTU), Singapore, which I joined in August 2026.
  </p>

  <h2>Research</h2>
  <p>
    My current research interests lie in computational 
    condensed matter physics with a focus on first-principles modeling of 2D magnetic materials, 
    multiferroics, and their heterostructures to explore their electronic structure, structural, 
    and magnetic properties, and potential emerging applications.
  </p>

  <h2>Background</h2>
  <p>
    I completed my MSc in Physics (Materials Science, Computation and
    Condensed Matter Theory) and my BTech in Technical and Applied Physics at
    The Technical University of Kenya, where I later worked as a research
    assistant and mentored undergraduate projects. I have also trained with
    the SIESTA community through the East African School on DFT and the CECAM
    "First steps with SIESTA" school.
  </p>

  <h2>Tools I use</h2>
  <p>
    SIESTA, Quantum ESPRESSO, VASP, Phonopy, Phono3py, BoltzTraP, Python, and
    Linux-based high-performance computing environments.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>